     "id": "p015.s01",
     "source": "BIANKI’S VISION"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p015"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p016.s01",
     "source": "(Kiowa Drawing)"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p016"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p017.s01",
     "source": "The ghost-dance among the Sioux was based on the belief that the dead Indians would all come to life and drive out the white intruders."
    },
    {
     "id": "p017.s02",
     "source": "Then the buffaloes, which were disappearing, would come back in the immense herds of the olden time."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p017"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p018.s01",
     "source": "The vision of one of the dreamer priests is represented."
    },
    {
     "id": "p018.s02",
     "source": "After reaching the spirit world, Bianki found himself on a vast prairie covered with innumerable buffaloes and ponies."
    },
    {
     "id": "p018.s03",
     "source": "He went through the herds (dotted lines) until he came to a large Kiowa camp, with its ornament tepees."
    },
    {
     "id": "p018.s04",
     "source": "He met four young women who had died years before, and asked about two of his brothers, also dead."
    },
    {
     "id": "p018.s05",
     "source": "He soon met them coming into camp, with buffalo meat hanging from their saddles."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p018"
  },
